{"name":"Lipstick","hex":"#c95b83","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lipstick","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Makeup for the lips.","A stick of this makeup."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply lipstick to; to paint with lipstick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lipstick","blocks":[{"text":"Lipstick is a cosmetic product used to apply color and texture to lips, often made of wax and oil. Different pigments are used to produce color, and minerals such as silica may be used to provide texture. The use of lipstick dates back to early civilizations such as Sumer and the Indus Valley Civilisation, and was popularized in the Western world in the 16th century. Some lipsticks contain traces of toxic materials, such as lead and PFAS, which prompted health concerns and regulation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/330px-Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipstick","wikidata":"Q184191"},{"title":"Lipstick (1976 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lipstick is a 1976 American rape and revenge thriller film directed by Lamont Johnson and starring Margaux Hemingway, Chris Sarandon, Perry King, and Anne Bancroft. Mariel Hemingway also has a supporting role as Margaux's onscreen sister. The film follows a fashion model who is raped by her teenage sister's music teacher. Upon his acquittal in court, he rapes her sister, leading her to enact a brutal revenge."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/LipstickFilm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipstick_(1976_film)","wikidata":"Q1768442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Magenta_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/5